,title,link,text,language,family
0,Yabula-Yabula language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yabula-Yabula_language,"Yabula-Yabula (Jabulajabula) in an extinct language of Australia, located in Victoria and New South Wales. Dixon listed it an isolate, but Glottolog evaluates it as a dialect of Yotayota. [2]",Yabula Yabula,Australian
1,Yotayotic languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yotayotic_languages,"The Yotayotic languages are a pair of languages of the Pama-Nyungan family, Yotayota and Yabula-Yabula. [1] Dixon (2002) classified them as two separate families, but per Bowe & Morey (1999) [2] Glottolog considers them to be dialects of a single language.",Yabula Yabula,Australian
2,"Yabula Yabula Language (YXY) - L1 & L2 Speakers, Status, Map ...",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/yxy/,"Explore Yabula Yabula and 226 other languages used in Australia with Ethnologue: Languages of Australia —a downloadable PDF document that provides detailed analysis presented in formats not available in the online version of Ethnologue. It includes: Comprehensive country overview. Statistical summaries by language status, size, and family.",Yabula Yabula,Australian
3,Yabula-Yabula language explained,https://everything.explained.today/Yabula-Yabula_language/,"Yabula-Yabula (Jabulajabula) in an extinct language of Australia, located in Victoria and New South Wales. Dixon listed it an isolate, but Glottolog evaluates it as a dialect of Yotayota. [1]",Yabula Yabula,Australian
4,Yabula-Yabula language Facts for Kids,https://kids.kiddle.co/Yabula-Yabula_language,What is the Yabula-Yabula Language? Yabula-Yabula was an Aboriginal Australian language. It belonged to the rich history of languages spoken by Indigenous Australians. Languages like Yabula-Yabula are very important. They help us understand the culture and history of the people who spoke them.,Yabula Yabula,Australian
5,Amano Yabula Noko Wemwana Niwe Nyatumbe? - AllMusic,https://www.allmusic.com/song/amano-yabula-noko-wemwana-niwe-nyatumbe--mt0061110001,"Explore Amano Yabula Noko Wemwana Niwe Nyatumbe? by Steve Tsotsi Kasumali & 2 Friends. Get track information, read reviews, listen to it streaming,...",Yabula Yabula,Australian
6,The Yorta Yorta (Bangerang) Language of the Murray Goulburn Including ...,https://openresearch-repository.anu.edu.au/server/api/core/bitstreams/c0ddf545-58b8-46a9-a087-fb46f254b7d5/content,"The Yabula Yabula language, however, has much less similarity and in statistical terms might seem to be a separate language. Hercus (1 986:239) reports that her informants regarded Yabula Yabula as the closest relative or even a subdivision of Yorta Yorta.",Yabula Yabula,Australian
7,"Book, Heather Bowe et al, Yorta Yorta language heritage, 1997",https://victoriancollections.net.au/items/56c69087400d0c3518d14be8,"Physical description An account of the Yorta Yorta language, with a full Yorta Yorta-English dictionary, a detailed grammar section, background information about previous language revival projects, hymns, historical records and place names. A chapter devoted to Yabula Yabula is also included. Inscriptions & markings Maps, b&w photographs, dictionary, word lists, worksheets,",Yabula Yabula,Australian
8,"Book, Bowe, Heather et al, Yorta Yorta language heritage, 1997",https://victoriancollections.net.au/items/603c856481449253daf26dd6,The book uses early historical records and spoken resources to document the language heritage of the Yorta Yorta ; includes Yorta Yorta grammar and English to Yorta Yorta and Yorta Yorta to English dictionaries ; also includes a Yabula Yabula grammar and vocabulary list ; Yorta Yorta language revival project.,Yabula Yabula,Australian
